{"id":"sw-9b9cf3","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Why\n\nM0 reshapes the engine core (thread split, lifecycle, channels). ~2.5k LoC of disconnected voxel machinery and an orphaned crate sit in the blast radius. Per the design decision: unencumbered by what exists — delete is fast. The voxel machinery returns later **redesigned per `docs/voxel-plugin-design.md`** (V1–V9); nothing deleted here is the future implementation.\n\n## Current state\n\nUnreferenced from the live frame path (survey 2026-08-11): `raymarcher.rs` (772), `brick_pager.rs` (748), `svo.rs` (573), `brick_pool.rs` (364), `bvh.rs` (218), `voxel_object.rs` (191), `brick_index.rs` (118), `brick_source.rs`, `brick_data.rs`, plus `shaders/raymarch.wgsl` (33k) and `shaders/blit.wgsl`. `crates/sandbox_old` exists on disk outside the workspace (10 files, old egui overlay). `gpu_timing.rs` is also orphaned but is **kept** — it gets wired in the M0 profiling story.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Orphan modules and their shaders deleted; `lib.rs` and `Cargo.toml` deps pruned accordingly (`gltf`? stays — `assets.rs` is live)\n- [ ] `crates/sandbox_old` deleted\n- [ ] Workspace deps trimmed to what member crates consume (egui may stay declared only if a member uses it)\n- [ ] `cargo build` + `cargo clippy` clean across the workspace; sandbox still runs","estimate":2,"labels":["M0","improvement"],"sort_order":"a0","title":"Purge orphan modules and sandbox_old"},"created_at":"2026-08-11T19:24:24.741245Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.227 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-ca0d9b","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Why\n\nThe entry point exists but is thin: `App` has only `update`, `EngineConfig` predates the design, and there is no `GameContext` or `WindowState`. This story brings the game-facing lifecycle to the shape in `docs/architecture-design.md` (The App Trait / GameContext / Engine Entry Point).\n\n## Current state\n\n`engine.rs:481` — `trait App { fn update(\u0026mut self, engine: \u0026mut Engine, world: \u0026mut World, dt: f32); }`. `EngineConfig { title, window_mode, vsync, log_level, worker_threads }`. `App::update` receives `\u0026mut Engine` directly (leaks render-side state into game code — violates the firewall). Esc-to-exit is hardcoded in the engine event handler (`engine.rs:551`). No `WindowState`; `WindowMode::Fullscreen` hardcodes 1920×1080.\n\n## Target (per design doc)\n\n- `trait App { init, update, fixed_update, shutdown }` — engine calls `init` once after World creation; `shutdown` before exit (wired fully by the teardown story)\n- `GameContext\u003c'_\u003e` as the single game-facing borrow: `world`, `input`, `time`, `window` now; `assets`/`audio`/`events` fields arrive with their milestones. **Game code never sees `Engine`, `GpuContext`, or wgpu types**\n- `EngineConfig { title, window_mode, fixed_timestep, pipeline_mode, pacing: PacingConfig, render_budget, log_level }` — `pipeline_mode` enum defined with `Overlapped` implemented; `PacingConfig` minimal (`vsync` honored, rest fields present but inert until OQ 8 loops land)\n- `WindowState { width, height, scale_factor, focused, mode }` game-visible\n- Esc-to-exit removed from engine; the sandbox decides its own quit binding (via a `GameContext` quit request)\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Sandbox compiles against the new `App` + `GameContext` shape with no `Engine`/wgpu types in game code\n- [ ] `init` runs exactly once before the first `update`; `shutdown` runs on exit\n- [ ] `WindowState` reflects live size/scale/focus\n- [ ] Fullscreen mode uses the actual monitor mode, not hardcoded dimensions","estimate":3,"labels":["M0","feature"],"sort_order":"a1","title":"App lifecycle \u0026 EngineConfig to design shape"},"created_at":"2026-08-11T19:24:42.754559Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.227 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-fccf7b","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Why\n\n`Capabilities` (sw-e06087) is essentially done — probed at boot, elevated limits, feature negotiation, log summary. A few fields diverge from the design contract, and two capability flags the architecture now depends on are missing.\n\n## Current state\n\n`gpu.rs:16` — probes `int64_atomics` via `SHADER_INT64_ATOMIC_ALL_OPS` only; no `texture_int64_atomic`; field named `min_ubo_align`; has useful extras the design lacks (`shader_i16`, `hdr_color_spaces`, `max_ssbo_binding_mb`, `adapter_name`, `backend`) — keep those.\n\n## Target (per design doc — Capabilities)\n\n- Add `int64_atomic_min_max` (probe `SHADER_INT64_ATOMIC_MIN_MAX` — the Nanite-atomics gate for the OQ 1/OQ 7 visibility-buffer tier; on Metal requires Apple-M2-class) **distinct from** `int64_atomic_all_ops`\n- Add `texture_int64_atomic` (probe `TEXTURE_INT64_ATOMIC`)\n- Rename `min_ubo_align` → `min_ubo_alignment` to match the doc\n- Keep the extra fields; update `log_summary()` to include the new flags\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Struct matches the design contract as a superset (doc fields all present, doc names)\n- [ ] Both new features negotiated opt-in-if-available like the existing seven\n- [ ] Boot log shows the new flags; headless probe still works","estimate":1,"labels":["M0","feature"],"sort_order":"a2","title":"Align Capabilities probe with design contract"},"created_at":"2026-08-11T19:24:55.037732Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.227 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-64ef40","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-64ef40","target_id":"sw-ca0d9b"}],"description":"## Why\n\nTime today is two lines: a raw `Instant` delta on `AppRunnerState` handed to `update`. The design requires a `Time` struct and the fixed-tick machinery that physics, determinism (OQ 19), and interpolation (OQ 6) all stand on.\n\n## Current state\n\n`engine.rs:498` — `last_frame: Instant`, unclamped `dt`. No elapsed, no frame counter, no accumulator, no `fixed_update` calls (the hook arrives with the App-lifecycle story).\n\n## Target (per design doc — GameContext / The App Trait)\n\n- `Time { dt: f32, elapsed: f64, frame: u64, fixed_dt: f32 }` in `GameContext`\n- `dt` clamped (spiral-of-death guard: cap accumulated debt, e.g. max 0.25 s)\n- Fixed accumulator: `fixed_update` runs 0–N times per frame at `EngineConfig.fixed_timestep` (default 1/60), before `update`, per the frame lifecycle table (INPUT → FIXED → UPDATE)\n- Accumulator alpha exposed engine-internally (the extract-time interpolation contract consumes it in M2 — not implemented here, but the value must exist)\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `fixed_update` fires at the configured rate independent of render rate (verify at uncapped and artificially throttled frame rates)\n- [ ] `dt` clamp prevents accumulator spiral after a long stall (e.g. window drag)\n- [ ] `Time.elapsed`/`frame` monotonically correct; unit tests for the accumulator math","estimate":2,"labels":["M0","feature"],"sort_order":"a3","title":"Time struct + fixed-timestep accumulator"},"created_at":"2026-08-11T19:25:08.198546Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.227 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-a6bcd7","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-a6bcd7","target_id":"sw-ca0d9b"},{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-a6bcd7","target_id":"sw-9b9cf3"}],"description":"## Why\n\nThe load-bearing M0 story. Today everything — event pump, `App::update`, cull, stream, encode, submit, present — runs on the main thread inside the winit callback. The design's foundational contract is the two-thread split with owned-value channel handoff (Frame Pipeline Architecture; Lifecycle — The Control Channel).\n\n## Current state\n\n`engine.rs` — single-threaded; `Engine` owns game state (`input`, `view`) *and* render state (`gpu`, `display`, passes) in one struct, so the split forces a type-level cut through `Engine`. No `FramePacket`, no channels of any kind between game and render. `StreamOutput\u003c'a\u003e` borrows and cannot cross threads. Surface `Outdated`/`Lost` reconfigures then **drops the frame** without retry, after cull/stream work is already spent.\n\n## Target (per design doc)\n\n- **Main thread = Game Thread** (winit event loop stays here, platform requirement); **dedicated Render Thread** owns `GpuContext`, `DisplaySurface`, passes, render targets\n- **Packet channel**, bounded(1): minimal `FramePacket { frame_index, views: Vec\u003cViewParams\u003e }` with a single Main view — real draw data arrives with M1's delta extract\n- **Feedback channel**: minimal `FrameFeedback { frame_index }` (readback ring is M1+)\n- **Control channel (OOB)**: `Resized`, `ScaleFactorChanged`, `Quit` — drained at the top of RECEIVE, applied at frame boundaries only (transport OOB, application frame-synchronized)\n- Render loop: drain control → recv packet → (temporary) clear-color frame → present. Surface `Outdated`/`Lost` at acquire → reconfigure + retry **once**, else skip present — no crash path\n- Channel-closure is the shutdown backstop signal (teardown story completes the protocol)\n- `PipelineMode::Overlapped` semantics: game thread computes N+1 while render draws N; the bounded channel is the throttle\n\n## Accepted temporary regression\n\nThe existing gbuffer/lighting mesh path **cannot** run on the render thread without the M1 extract/retained-scene work (it borrows `World` directly). During M0 the presented frame is clear-color only; the pass code stays compiled but unwired. M1 restores meshes through the proper contract. This is deliberate — do not bridge `World` across threads to keep the old path alive.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Game and render threads run concurrently (profiling lanes show overlap once the profiling story lands)\n- [ ] Window shows engine clear color; resize via control channel reconfigures without crash or deadlock; rapid resize storms survive (latest-wins)\n- [ ] No `World`, `Input`, or game-side type crosses to the render thread; no `wgpu` type remains on the game side\n- [ ] Quit via control channel or window close exits cleanly (full ordering in the teardown story)\n- [ ] Bounded channel verified: game thread blocks on send when render is slow (test with artificial render stall)","estimate":8,"labels":["M0","feature"],"sort_order":"a4","title":"Game/Render thread split with packet, feedback, and control channels"},"created_at":"2026-08-11T19:25:28.766925Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.227 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-c1320b","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-c1320b","target_id":"sw-a6bcd7"}],"description":"## Why\n\n\"Profiling lanes from the first commit\" is one of the four day-one golden rules (Critical Path) — every later milestone is validated through them. Currently the weakest area: zero CPU instrumentation, no profiler crates, and `gpu_timing.rs` written but wired to nothing (every `timestamp_writes:` in the live passes is `None`).\n\n## Current state\n\n`gpu_timing.rs` (129 LoC, orphan): complete query-set/resolve/readback API with EMA averages and the Apple begin-timestamp workaround — but `read_results` does a **blocking** `poll(wait_indefinitely)`, which violates the never-block rule (Render-to-Game Feedback). No `tracy`/`profiling`/`puffin` in any Cargo.toml. Worker threads are already named (`sw-worker-{i}`).\n\n## Target (per design doc — Profiling \u0026 Instrumentation, OQ 24)\n\n- `profile_scope!`, `counter!`, `gauge!` macros — zero-cost no-ops in shipping builds (feature-gated); the `profiling`-crate facade pattern is acceptable as the base\n- **Tracy sink** behind a dev feature: zones, frame marks; named lanes registered for Game, Render, and both worker pools (Streaming Coordinator/Audio/IO lanes register when those threads exist)\n- Wire `gpu_timing.rs` into the render thread's passes (clear pass now; every pass as M1 adds them), with `read_results` made **non-blocking** (poll without wait; results surface 1–N frames late — the readback-ring shape in miniature). Feed pass timings into Tracy's GPU context\n- `BudgetRegistry` skeleton: type + registration API only (the egui budget table is M3)\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Tracy capture shows Game and Render lanes overlapping (proves the Overlapped pipeline), worker lanes named, frame marks per frame\n- [ ] GPU pass timings appear in Tracy's GPU timeline; no blocking waits anywhere on the render thread (verify by timing the read path)\n- [ ] Shipping-profile build compiles the macros to nothing (assert via a feature-off build)\n- [ ] `counter!`/`gauge!` round-trip to Tracy plots","estimate":5,"labels":["M0","feature"],"sort_order":"a5","title":"Profiling foundation — scope macros, Tracy, thread lanes, GPU timestamps"},"created_at":"2026-08-11T19:25:45.122378Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.227 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-601a0f","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-601a0f","target_id":"sw-a6bcd7"}],"description":"## Why\n\nShutdown today is \"the event loop exits and Rust drops things in whatever order\" — no `App::shutdown`, no GPU quiesce, no thread joins. The Lifecycle section (OQ 15) specifies a five-stage protocol; M0 implements the stages that exist yet (streaming/audio join in later milestones), establishing the ordering discipline before more threads arrive.\n\n## Current state\n\n`engine.rs:544/551` — `event_loop.exit()` on CloseRequested/Esc, then implicit `Drop`. Only `impl Drop` in the workspace was the (now-purged) `BrickPager`. No `device.poll` wait, no channel-closure signaling, no join of the rayon pools.\n\n## Target (per design doc — Lifecycle, Teardown Protocol; M0 subset)\n\n1. **Stop simulation**: exit main loop; run `App::shutdown` while services live\n2. **Drain the pipeline**: close packet + control channels (closure = the backstop signal); render thread finishes in-flight frames and exits its loop; GPU wait-idle; (readback drains once profiling story lands)\n3. **Stop services**: worker pools join\n4. **Destroy**: GPU resources → device → window → process exit (`Engine::run` still returns per current signature; `-\u003e !` conversion optional here)\n- Per-stage deadline (~2 s) → log + force; the process must never hang on exit\n- `Quit` arrives via the control channel (window close or game-requested through `GameContext`)\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Clean exit path: shutdown hook runs exactly once, threads join, no wgpu validation errors or leaks on exit (run with wgpu validation on)\n- [ ] Killing the render thread's channel mid-frame does not deadlock the game thread (backstop verified)\n- [ ] Deadline forcing works: an artificially-hung stage logs and exits within the deadline\n- [ ] Repeated launch/quit cycles (10×) leak-free and hang-free","estimate":3,"labels":["M0","feature"],"sort_order":"a6","title":"Minimal staged teardown \u0026 clean exit"},"created_at":"2026-08-11T19:25:59.7446Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.227 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-64ef40","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"## Why\n\nTime today is two lines: a raw `Instant` delta on `AppRunnerState` handed to `update`. The design requires a `Time` struct and the fixed-tick machinery that physics, determinism (OQ 19), interpolation (OQ 6), and pause/time-scale (OQ 33) all stand on.\n\n## Current state\n\n`engine.rs:498` — `last_frame: Instant`, unclamped `dt`. No elapsed, no frame counter, no accumulator, no `fixed_update` calls (the hook arrives with the App-lifecycle story).\n\n## Target (per design doc — GameContext / The App Trait / Worlds \u0026 Game Flow, OQ 33)\n\n- `Time { dt: f32, real_dt: f32, elapsed: f64, frame: u64, fixed_dt: f32, scale: f32, paused: bool }` in `GameContext` — the full OQ 33 shape from day one (contract-shaped golden rule; fields are cheap now, a retrofit isn't)\n- `dt` = **scaled** delta (0 while paused); `real_dt` = unscaled wall-clock (UI reads this)\n- `dt` clamped (spiral-of-death guard: cap accumulated debt, e.g. max 0.25 s)\n- Fixed accumulator: `fixed_update` runs 0–N times per frame at `EngineConfig.fixed_timestep` (default 1/60), before `update`, per the frame lifecycle table (INPUT → FIXED → UPDATE)\n- **Accumulator advances by scaled time**: `paused` freezes it (zero ticks), `scale \u003c 1` is slow-motion with per-tick determinism intact — implement the semantics now, they're a few lines inside the accumulator\n- `set_paused()` / `set_time_scale()` on `GameContext`\n- Accumulator alpha exposed engine-internally (the extract-time interpolation contract consumes it in M2 — not implemented here, but the value must exist)\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `fixed_update` fires at the configured rate independent of render rate (verify at uncapped and artificially throttled frame rates)\n- [ ] `paused = true` → zero fixed ticks, `dt == 0`, `real_dt` still advances; `scale = 0.5` → half the fixed ticks per wall-second\n- [ ] `dt` clamp prevents accumulator spiral after a long stall (e.g. window drag)\n- [ ] `Time.elapsed`/`frame` monotonically correct; unit tests for accumulator math including pause/scale transitions mid-frame"},"created_at":"2026-08-12T06:54:53.899492Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.227 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-ca0d9b","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"## Why\n\nThe entry point exists but is thin: `App` has only `update`, `EngineConfig` predates the design, and there is no `GameContext` or `WindowState`. This story brings the game-facing lifecycle to the shape in `docs/architecture-design.md` (The App Trait / GameContext / Engine Entry Point).\n\n## Current state\n\n`engine.rs:481` — `trait App { fn update(\u0026mut self, engine: \u0026mut Engine, world: \u0026mut World, dt: f32); }`. `EngineConfig { title, window_mode, vsync, log_level, worker_threads }`. `App::update` receives `\u0026mut Engine` directly (leaks render-side state into game code — violates the firewall). Esc-to-exit is hardcoded in the engine event handler (`engine.rs:551`). No `WindowState`; `WindowMode::Fullscreen` hardcodes 1920×1080.\n\n## Target (per design doc)\n\n- `trait App { init, update, fixed_update, shutdown }` — engine calls `init` once after World creation; `shutdown` before exit (wired fully by the teardown story)\n- `GameContext\u003c'_\u003e` as the single game-facing borrow: `world`, `input`, `time`, `window` now; `assets`/`audio`/`events` fields arrive with their milestones. **Game code never sees `Engine`, `GpuContext`, or wgpu types**\n- `EngineConfig { title, window_mode, fixed_timestep, pipeline_mode, pacing: PacingConfig, render_budget, log_level }` — `pipeline_mode` enum defined with `Overlapped` implemented; `PacingConfig` minimal (`vsync` honored, rest fields present but inert until OQ 8 loops land). **`EngineConfig` = initial values only** (OQ 33): runtime mutation arrives via `GameContext` setters (`set_pacing`/`set_window_mode` — signatures may be stubbed in M0, wired when the control-channel resize path lands)\n- `WindowState { width, height, scale_factor, focused, mode }` game-visible\n- Esc-to-exit removed from engine; the sandbox decides its own quit binding (via a `GameContext` quit request)\n- Not in M0 scope (design exists, later milestones): world load/swap methods (OQ 33), action mapping (OQ 34 — M2 with Input work)\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Sandbox compiles against the new `App` + `GameContext` shape with no `Engine`/wgpu types in game code\n- [ ] `init` runs exactly once before the first `update`; `shutdown` runs on exit\n- [ ] `WindowState` reflects live size/scale/focus\n- [ ] Fullscreen mode uses the actual monitor mode, not hardcoded dimensions"},"created_at":"2026-08-12T06:55:11.064872Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.227 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
